WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:10.539
Vinnie was taken to the home of the boy, Dag.

2
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.746
His house had stone walls and a roof made of straw.

3
00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:19.210
His mother and sister, Birgitta, were inside.

4
00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:25.015
Dag explained what happened.

5
00:00:25.016 --> 00:00:29.533
Dag and Gunnar laid Vinnie down on a bench.

6
00:00:29.534 --> 00:00:32.497
It was covered with bear skins.

7
00:00:32.498 --> 00:00:35.609
Dag's mother hurried over to Vinnie.

8
00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:42.344
"Birgitta, bring me the whale bone," she said.

9
00:00:42.345 --> 00:00:47.684
"Whale bone?" asked Mandy. "What is that for?

10
00:00:47.685 --> 00:00:50.538
Is Vinnie going to be okay?"

11
00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:54.333
"Don't worry," said Dag's mother.

12
00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:59.076
"There are magic symbols carved into the whale bone.

13
00:00:59.077 --> 00:01:02.468
It will help your brother heal quickly."

14
00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:06.373
Birgitta gave the whale bone to her mother.

15
00:01:06.374 --> 00:01:11.095
Her mother placed it under the bear skins beneath Vinnie.

16
00:01:11.096 --> 00:01:16.230
Vikings believed that symbols had magical power.

17
00:01:16.231 --> 00:01:20.375
Soon after, Vinnie opened his eyes.

18
00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:24.341
"Oh, my head," he groaned.

19
00:01:24.342 --> 00:01:27.615
There was a big bump on his forehead.

20
00:01:27.616 --> 00:01:29.469
He tried to sit up.

21
00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.446
"Where am I?

22
00:01:31.447 --> 00:01:33.626
Where's my sister?"

23
00:01:33.627 --> 00:01:37.017
Mandy knelt down beside Vinnie.

24
00:01:37.018 --> 00:01:40.097
"Are you okay?" she asked.

25
00:01:40.098 --> 00:01:44.333
"Except for a headache, yes," he replied.

26
00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:47.936
Mandy turned to Birgitta and Dag's mother.

27
00:01:47.937 --> 00:01:53.346
"Thank you so much," she said.

28
00:01:53.347 --> 00:01:59.939
Now that Vinnie seemed better, Mandy looked at the inside of the house more closely.

29
00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:04.425
It was just one long room with no windows.

30
00:02:04.426 --> 00:02:08.114
In the middle of the room was a fireplace.

31
00:02:08.115 --> 00:02:18.814
She was surprised to see animals—a cow, two sheep, and four pigs—in a pen at the far end of the house.

32
00:02:18.815 --> 00:02:23.819
"Why do the animals live in your house?" she asked Birgitta.

33
00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:28.616
"It's too cold to keep them outdoors," she explained.

34
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:32.873
"And having them inside keeps us warm too."

35
00:02:32.874 --> 00:02:39.333
"Birgitta," called her mother, "take this soup to our old neighbor Hilda.

36
00:02:39.334 --> 00:02:42.276
She's been sick for three days."

37
00:02:42.277 --> 00:02:44.941
Birgitta took the pot of soup.

38
00:02:44.942 --> 00:02:48.537
"Come with me," she said to Mandy.

39
00:02:48.538 --> 00:02:55.074
While the girls were gone, Vinnie watched Gunnar practice sword fighting with Dag.

40
00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.805
They used wooden swords.

41
00:02:57.806 --> 00:03:03.478
"Gunnar, do you really want to be a warrior?" asked Vinnie.

42
00:03:03.479 --> 00:03:06.601
"Yes, I do," Gunnar said.

43
00:03:06.602 --> 00:03:10.336
"I practice my fighting skills whenever I can.

44
00:03:10.337 --> 00:03:14.075
There is nothing better than being a Viking warrior.

45
00:03:14.076 --> 00:03:17.156
I want to be the next Leif Erikson!"

46
00:03:17.157 --> 00:03:19.747
"Who's that?" asked Vinnie.

47
00:03:19.748 --> 00:03:24.350
"You don't know about him?" said Gunnar, surprised.

48
00:03:24.351 --> 00:03:27.678
"He's one of our most famous explorers.

49
00:03:27.679 --> 00:03:32.352
Leif Erikson discovered a new land far across the sea.

50
00:03:32.353 --> 00:03:35.146
He and his men saw many forests.

51
00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:38.556
The wood was perfect for building longships.

52
00:03:38.557 --> 00:03:44.345
They said the fish were bigger than me!"

53
00:03:44.346 --> 00:03:46.609
Vinnie and Gunnar laughed.

54
00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.414
Then they heard a loud noise at the door.

55
00:03:50.415 --> 00:03:56.233
"I finally found you little ship rats!" yelled Skull-Crusher.

56
00:03:56.234 --> 00:04:00.882
"My Captain!" Gunnar bowed his head.

57
00:04:00.883 --> 00:04:04.403
The red-faced captain stood in the doorway.

58
00:04:04.404 --> 00:04:07.076
He was very angry.

59
00:04:07.077 --> 00:04:14.650
"Where is my good-luck charm?" Skull-Crusher demanded.
